  - clueId: L09_LotusLeaf_Ratio
    title: Lotus Leaf - Ratio Clue
    content: Lotus leaf works best in a very small amount.
    relatedIngredients:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: d9e3e41cc52bba94997680b94ac53836, type: 2}
    relatedDimension: 2
  - clueId: L09_LotusLeaf_Combination
    title: Lotus Leaf - Combination Clue
    content: "Lotus leaf can be paired with glutinous rice, but black sesame is too strong for it."
    relatedIngredients:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: d9e3e41cc52bba94997680b94ac53836, type: 2}
    relatedDimension: 3
  - clueId: L09_LotusLeaf_Order
    title: Lotus Leaf - Order Clue
    content: "Add lotus leaf near the end. If it is used too early, its fresh flavor gets covered."
    relatedIngredients:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: d9e3e41cc52bba94997680b94ac53836, type: 2}
    relatedDimension: 1
  fallbackHintText: No new hint for now. Keep what worked
  progressiveHintRules:
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_RedBean_Ratio
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Red bean should be the largest amount. It is the base of this recipe.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_LotusLeaf_Ratio
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Lotus leaf should be the smallest amount. It is light and easy to cover.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_Rice_Lotus_Combination
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Glutinous rice can hold the lotus leaf flavor. Add lotus leaf right after glutinous rice in the same batch.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_Sesame_Lotus_Combination
    priority: 19
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Black sesame is strong. Keep it separate from lotus leaf.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_RedBean_Order
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Red bean should go first. It builds the base.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_LotusLeaf_Order
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Lotus leaf should come right after glutinous rice, in the same batch.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_Middle_Order
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: After red bean, add glutinous rice, then lotus leaf in that same batch. Add black sesame after that in its own batch.
